<title>PAKISTAN: U.S. to give Pakistan $20 mln for wheat import.</title>
<headline>U.S. to give Pakistan $20 mln for wheat import.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States will give Pakistan a credit of $20 million wheat import under an agreement signed in Islamabad on Wednesday, a Pakistan government statement said.</p>
<p>It said the credit had been extended by the Commodity Credit Corporation of the U.S. Department of Agriculture under Washington's PL-480 (food-for-peace) programme.</p>
<p>&quot;The proceeds from the sale of wheat imported under this special programme can be used for agricultural research and development and to help promote efficiency and modernisation among local wheat producers and distributors,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Wednesday's agreement adds $20 million in wheat support to an existing $10 million U.S. assistance to Pakistan for soymeal for which the two governments signed an agreement on June 30, the statement said.</p>
